  "answer": "Call 911 now. A child who is floppy and drowsy after a seizure needs emergency care, even if the shaking has stopped. Lay them on their side, put nothing in their mouth, and stay with them.",
  "triage": "Call 911 now and do not wait to see if they perk up. Tell them if the shaking starts again, or if the lips or face turn blue or breathing is hard. Health811 is for nurse advice later, not for this moment.",
  "sources": ["MyHealth Alberta", "Children's Hospital of Philadelphia (CHOP)", "Mayo Clinic", "Cleveland Clinic", "Epilepsy Foundation"]
}
